

# Auracle API

## Overview

The Auracle API provides both REST and WebSocket interfaces for interacting with our services. The REST API follows standard HTTP conventions and supports both Prime and Sovereign tiers, while the WebSocket API enables real-time data exchange.
# Connection Details

## Base URL

Assuming your Auracle URL is https://test.auracle.digital/, your corresponding WebSocket URL would be: wss://test-backend.auracle.digital/v1.

The backend service adheres to the same IP whitelist policies as the front-end service. If you need to add (static) IP addresses to the whitelist, please contact our support team.

## Pricing
## JSON-RPC Schema


| Name   | Type   | Description |
--------|--------|-------------
|jsonrpc | string | Only "2.0" is supported |
|id      | string | This will be echoed back in responses or subscription payloads|
|method  | string | Establishing the specific API to connect to. Documented below |
|params  | string | Details regarding the specific API call. Documented below     |


# About

## Introduction

Auracle is a high-performance decentralized oracle system built on Cosmos SDK that bridges blockchain networks with trusted real-world data. Our platform provides secure, low-latency data feeds from markets, sensors, and other real-time sources with industry-leading 5-second finality, enabling developers to build robust blockchain applications with reliable access to off-chain information.

## Product Offerings

### Auracle Prime
Enterprise-focused hybrid architecture combining controlled off-chain processing with on-chain verification. This solution ensures maximum security while providing full in-house control for enterprise clients with specific compliance and reliability requirements.

### Auracle Sovereign
Fully decentralized network where independent nodes and stakers participate in distributed data sourcing. This permissionless solution is secured by crypto-economic incentives and cryptographic verification mechanisms, ideal for public blockchain applications.

## Key Technical Features

- Native Cosmos Integration: Built on Cosmos SDK with full IBC (Inter-Blockchain Communication) compatibility
- Flexible Deployment Options: Available as hybrid or fully permissionless implementations
- High Performance: 5-second finality for near real-time data availability
- Complete Infrastructure Ownership: End-to-end control of the oracle stack
- Extensive Connectivity: Integrations with 96+ centralized exchanges, 124+ DeFi protocols, and major blockchain networks

## System Architecture

### Oracle Engine
- Continuously polls external data sources (APIs, IoT)
- Validates, aggregates, and cryptographically signs data

### Blockchain Infrastructure
- Permissioned Tendermint-based consensus
- Validator nodes execute CosmWasm smart contracts
- IBC enables cross-chain interoperability

### Data Processing & Security
- Digital signatures with stored public keys
- Strict data validation (timestamps, value ranges)
- Immutable ledger transactions for auditability

### User Access & Management
- REST APIs for querying validated on-chain data
- Secure transmission via TLS/SSL
- Identity management with ACLs and cryptographic access control

## Data Flow Process

1. Data Acquisition: Oracle Engine fetches data from external sources
2. Cryptographic Signing: Data payloads are cryptographically signed
3. Transaction Submission: Signed data submitted via Cosmos SDK
4. On-chain Validation: CosmWasm contracts verify digital signatures
5. Immutable Storage: Validated data stored on the blockchain
6. Secure Distribution: External applications access data through API Gateway

## Business Model

- Tiered subscription model based on data frequency, volume, and types
- Custom enterprise solutions with dedicated oracle implementation
- AURO token economy for governance and incentives

## Getting Started

The Auracle API documentation provides detailed information on how to integrate our oracle services into your blockchain applications. For enterprise solutions or custom implementations, please contact our sales team.

