#Audit Logs & Usage (Prime + Sovereign)
##Logs

Retrieve audit logs with query parameters for start and end time.

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "unique-request-id",
  "method": "Logs",
  "params": {
    "start": 1685294400,
    "end": 1685373600
  }
}
```

### Request
| Name  | Type    | Description                                 |
| ----- | ------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| start | integer | Unix timestamp (seconds) for the start time |
| end   | integer | Unix timestamp (seconds) for the end time   |


```json
{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": "f1986b5d-a8b7-47a2-9333-e2f123dca9b6",
    "result": [
      {
        "log_id": "log_12345",
        "timestamp": 1685300000,
        "action": "API call",
        "user_id": "user_6789",
        "details": "Accessed feed data"
      },
      {
        "log_id": "log_67890",
        "timestamp": 1685360000,
        "action": "API call",
        "user_id": "user_2345",
        "details": "Created new subscription"
      }
    ]
        
}

```

### Response
| Name      | Type    | Description                              |
| --------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| log\_id   | string  | Unique identifier for the log entry      |
| timestamp | integer | Unix timestamp of the log entry          |
| action    | string  | Action taken (e.g., "API call", "login") |
| user\_id  | string  | User who performed the action            |
| details   | string  | Additional details about the action      |

##Usage

Retrieve API call breakdown by endpoint.


### Request


```json
{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": "f1986b5d-a8b7-47a2-9333-e2f123dca9b6",
    "result": {
      "/v1/feeds/{feedId}/latest": 120,
      "/v1/governance/proposals": 50,
      "/v1/webhooks": 75
    }
        
}

```

### Response
| Name     | Type    | Description                             |
| -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------- |
| endpoint | string  | API endpoint being tracked              |
| count    | integer | Number of times the endpoint was called |


## Error Handling

All errors follow this format:

```json
{
    "code": "INVALID_REQUEST",
    "message": "Invalid request parameters",
    "details": {
        "field": "amount",
        "reason": "must be positive"
    }
}
```

Common error codes:
- 400: Bad Request
- 401: Unauthorized
- 403: Forbidden
- 404: Not Found
- 429: Too Many Requests
- 500: Internal Server Error